+# v27 — continuous held map panning
+
+Gem Sniping now keeps the mouse button held while moving the map and checking
+fresh screenshots for the next fixed-route location. It stops movement at the
+first confirmed frame where that target is safely clickable, rather than
+continuing toward the map centre.
+
+- Start near the opposite edge to leave room for the intended map movement.
+  Revealing a lower location starts the mouse low and drags the map upward.
+- Measure progress after movements of at most 120 reference pixels, keeping
+  the same button hold across those screenshot/recognition checks.
+- Keep drag starts, cursor paths and target clicks within the user-marked map
+  outline, with padding around the legend, zoom controls, Back and region tabs.
+- Stop the cursor, hold it stationary for 0.18 seconds, then release. Confirm
+  the settled map again before clicking the next location.
+- At the window edge, release safely before re-anchoring for another stroke.
+  Recovery may also use separate strokes; a hold cannot extend past the window.
+- Release on F10, focus loss, resizing, obstruction, capture/recognition errors
+  or an unexpected map closure. Never click an unconfirmed target.
+
+Default and named routes, removals, history, settings, inspection waits and
+gem confirmation are retained from v26. This remains Windows mouse input and
+desktop screenshot capture. Keep BlueStacks visible, uncovered and focused.
+
+The Windows validation exercises actual held input and F10 release on the
+application's own test window. The full-route atlas benchmark uses simulated
+input, loading and empty detection; its results are not live BlueStacks times.
+
+Close the previous app, extract the complete folder and run its LoongLens.exe.
+Personal data stays in %LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens. The full 7z includes the EXE,
+source, assets, models, launchers, tests, tools and validation reports.
